=== 5. VERDICT ===
Session 50 item 2 is INVERTED, not merely unsupported:
  * the axis genuinely CAN see drive-dependence (thresholds 0.7-12.0 dB), so its verdict is meaningful;
  * but the shipped model's residual is 0.471 dB RMS, NOT the 0.094 dB the
    argument was built on — 5x larger and 3.3x the capture floor;
  * translated through the power curves that residual is equivalent to a MEDIAN
    3.5 dB of unmodelled drive-dependence, with 6 band(s) already inside
    the 4-19 dB range that pre-clipper elements deliver.

=> The drive axis does NOT say the missing element is drive-independent. Read
   correctly it says the opposite: there is several dB of drive-dependent residual
   the drive-independent model cannot absorb. The post-clipper restriction that has
   scoped A3 since session 50 rests on a residual figure I cannot reproduce, and at
   the reproducible figure the same argument points PRE-clipper.
   ⚠ This does not prove the carrier IS pre-clipper (see the upper-bound caveat in
   section 4) — it removes the reason for excluding it. Combined with session 52's
   proof that no causal linear POST-clipper element can supply the target, the
   pre-clipper region is now the only one not ruled out.
